---
import { pillars } from '../data/content';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section id="pillars" class="scroll-mt-24 border-y border-border bg-surface-sunken/40 py-16 sm:py-24">
	<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
			<p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-brand-teal uppercase">What it does</p>
			<h2
				class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance text-foreground sm:text-4xl"
			>
				Two jobs, and nothing else
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
				AgentGauge does not try to be a model, a proxy, or a second place to chat. It watches
				your limits, and optionally acts once a window rolls over.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
			{
				pillars.map((pillar, index) => (
					<article
						data-reveal
						style={`--reveal-delay:${index * 110}ms`}
						class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border/70 bg-surface-raised/70 p-7 backdrop-blur-md"
					>
						<span class="inline-flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-brand-ink text-background dark:bg-foreground dark:text-background">
							<Icon name={pillar.icon} class="size-5" />
						</span>
						<h3 class="mt-5 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">
							{pillar.title}
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{pillar.body}</p>
					</article>
				))
			}
		</div>

		<div
			data-reveal
			class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-amber/30 bg-brand-amber/5 p-6 backdrop-blur-md sm:p-7"
		>
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
				<Icon
					name="info"
					class="mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-brand-amber"
					aria-label="Important"
				/>
				<div>
					<h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-foreground">
						Nothing here can restart a window
					</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
						A prompt spends quota in whichever window is already active. It cannot start,
						restart, reset, or extend one — only the provider can do that. AgentGauge reads
						the reset timestamp the provider reports and, if you asked it to, sends one small
						Hi shortly afterwards. It spends quota, and it does not claim to have verified
						that a rollover happened.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
